<title>USA: Allied Capital sells 400,000 shrs.</title>
<headline>Allied Capital sells 400,000 shrs.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allied Capital Corp said it netted about $5.3 million, after expenses, after selling 400,000 shares of Allied Capital Lending Corp's common stock Thursday at $14 a share.</p>
<p>Allied Capital Corp said the shares it sold in the transaction represented about one-third of its holding in Allied Capital Lending. Lehman Brothers was the underwriter.</p>
<p>The company has been ordered by the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to sell all its Allied Capital Lending shares by December 1998, it said.</p>
<p>Allied Capital said it still owns 844,914 shares -- or about 16.5 percent -- of Allied Capital Lending's common stock.</p>
</text>
